### =====================================================================
### FoodRescue API - manual security test file (Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code REST Client)
###
### Passwords are NEVER stored in this file. Create a git-ignored file next to it,
### FoodRescue/http-client.env.json   (already listed in .gitignore):
###
###   {
###     "dev": {
###       "adminEmail": "<the AdminSeed:Email you configured>",
###       "adminPassword": "<the AdminSeed:Password you configured>"
###     }
###   }
###
### Run the requests from top to bottom. Expected status is written above each request.
### ===================================================================== 

@host = https://localhost:7295
@httpHost = http://localhost:5007
@password = Test-Passw0rd-123!

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. HTTPS: plain HTTP must be redirected (307/308) to https://localhost:7295
### EXPECT: 307 or 308, Location header starts with https://
### (turn off "follow redirects" in the client to see it)
GET {{httpHost}}/api/region

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Registration (EXPECT 200 first time, 409 when the e-mail already exists)
### Role is not part of the request - the server always creates Role=User.
### Registration only creates the user (no token in the response). The token comes from login (step 2).
# @name registerA
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User A",
  "email": "  User.A@Example.com ",
  "phone": "0501111111",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###
# EXPECT: 200 first time / 409 afterwards (same e-mail, different casing & spaces = same account)
# @name registerB
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User B",
  "email": "user.b@example.com",
  "phone": "0502222222",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Validation: short password -> 400 (with a "message" field), invalid e-mail -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X Y", "email": "not-an-email", "phone": "0503333333", "password": "short" }

### Mass-assignment: an extra "role" field must be ignored (user is created as Role=User)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hacker", "email": "hacker@example.com", "phone": "0504444444", "password": "{{password}}", "role": "Admin" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Login (EXPECT 200 + token, role, expiresAt)
# @name loginA
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "USER.A@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@tokenA = {{loginA.response.body.$.token}}

# @name loginB
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user.b@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@tokenB = {{loginB.response.body.$.token}}

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### Wrong password -> 401 { "message": "שם משתמש או סיסמה שגויים." } (same text for unknown e-mail)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user.a@example.com", "password": "wrong-password" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. No token -> 401
### EXPECT: 401
GET {{host}}/api/donations/my-supplier-donations

###
### EXPECT: 401
DELETE {{host}}/api/region/1

###
### EXPECT: 401
POST {{host}}/api/donations/analyze-image

### Public on purpose (registration forms) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/region

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Regular user on Admin endpoints -> 403
### EXPECT: 403
DELETE {{host}}/api/region/1
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

###
### EXPECT: 403
POST {{host}}/api/ngos/1/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
Content-Type: application/json

"reason"

###
### EXPECT: 403
GET {{host}}/api/matches
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

###
### EXPECT: 403 (map shows addresses/coordinates of everybody - Admin only)
GET {{host}}/api/map/all-entities
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

###
### EXPECT: 403 (NGO list is for Admin / approved volunteers only)
GET {{host}}/api/ngos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

###
### EXPECT: 403 - creating a donation on behalf of a supplier is Admin only.
### (CreateDonationDto has no SupplierId: a supplier's own donations always belong to the supplier in the token)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/suppliers/1/donations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "regionId": 1, "latitude": 32.08, "longitude": 34.78, "latestPickupTime": "18:00:00", "categories": [ { "categoryId": 1, "quantity": 1, "weightKg": 1 } ] }

### Same endpoints as Admin -> 200 / 204 / 404 (never 401/403)
### EXPECT: 200
GET {{host}}/api/ngos
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
### EXPECT: 200
GET {{host}}/api/map/all-entities
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. IDOR - two users. A creates a volunteer profile, B (no profile) must get 404, never 403/200.
### EXPECT: 200 first time / 409 afterwards
# @name createVolunteerA
POST {{host}}/api/volunteers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicleType": "Car",
  "maxCapacityKg": 50,
  "isAvailable": true,
  "currentLatitude": 32.08,
  "currentLongitude": 34.78,
  "idNumber": "000000018",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "driverLicenseNumber": "1234567",
  "driverLicenseExpiry": "2030-01-01"
}

###
### If you got 409, read the id once with: GET /api/volunteers/{any id} as user A and paste it here.
@volunteerAId = {{createVolunteerA.response.body.$.id}}

### A reads own profile -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/volunteers/{{volunteerAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

###
### B reads A's profile -> EXPECT: 404
GET {{host}}/api/volunteers/{{volunteerAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

###
### B reads A's availability -> EXPECT: 404
GET {{host}}/api/volunteers/{{volunteerAId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

###
### B overwrites A's availability -> EXPECT: 404
POST {{host}}/api/volunteers/{{volunteerAId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}
Content-Type: application/json

[]

###
### B asks for a supplier profile that is not B's -> EXPECT: 404 (same as an id that does not exist)
GET {{host}}/api/suppliers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

###
### Set these two in http-client.env.json if you have data: an existing donation and match
### (@donationId / @matchId), then B (not related to them, not an approved volunteer) -> EXPECT: 404
@donationId = 1
@matchId = 1

GET {{host}}/api/donations/{{donationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

###
### EXPECT: 404
GET {{host}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

###
### EXPECT: 404
POST {{host}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

###
### B edits / cancels a donation that is not B's -> EXPECT: 404 (same as an id that does not exist)
PUT {{host}}/api/donations/{{donationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "test" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Comments: author/createdAt/id from the client are ignored; target is checked
### EXPECT: 400 (both donationId and matchId)
POST {{host}}/api/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "hi", "donationId": 1, "matchId": 1 }

###
### EXPECT: 404 (user A is not related to the donation) - "author": "Someone Else" is ignored
POST {{host}}/api/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": 99, "author": "Someone Else", "createdAt": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z", "content": "hi", "donationId": {{donationId}} }

###
### EXPECT: 200 - only comments the user is allowed to see
GET {{host}}/api/comments/tree
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

###
### EXPECT: 403
GET {{host}}/api/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Unified error shape: every error is { status, message, code, errors? }
### EXPECT: 400 with code "ValidationFailed" and errors.idNumber (check digit)
POST {{host}}/api/volunteers/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Id",
  "email": "bad.id@example.com",
  "phone": "0501234567",
  "vehicleType": "Car",
  "maxCapacityKg": 50,
  "idNumber": "123456789",
  "driverLicenseNumber": "1234567",
  "driverLicenseExpiry": "2030-01-01",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. E-mail link for a volunteer request: one-time token, no login JWT
### EXPECT: 404 for a wrong / used token
POST {{host}}/api/matches/by-link
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "not-a-real-token" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. Admin: engine status (real numbers) and settings (stored in the DB, used by the engine)
### EXPECT: 200
GET {{host}}/api/matches/engine-status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
### EXPECT: 200 - the next engine run uses the new timeout
PUT {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "matchingTimeoutMinutes": 7 }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. Notification center of the logged-in user
### EXPECT: 200 (array; total in the X-Total-Count header)
GET {{host}}/api/notifications?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
